From 3a48eb87866a3b7036e2d2716a2de69a26407fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix mkdir/chdir/symlink/access plumbing, add mknod
 syscall support

- Fix analyzer/mod.rs: add missing match arms for Mkdir/Chdir/Symlink
  (non-exhaustive match, wouldn't compile)
- Fix codegen: set uses_files=true for Mkdir/Chdir/Symlink/FileAvailable
  so coreasm/x86_64/file.asm actually gets %included
- Add missing MKDIR/CHDIR/SYMLINK/FILE_AVAILABLE macros to file.asm
  (codegen referenced them but they didn't exist -> NASM assembly failure)
- Fix parse_symlink: target parsing used parse_primary(), which has an
  existing rule treating 'string' followed by 'to' as a function-call
  expression. This silently ate the 'to' keyword + linkpath. Now parses
  the target as a plain string/identifier instead.
- Fix tests/086_symlink_error.vox: symlink(2) allows dangling targets
  by design on Linux, so a nonexistent target never errors. Changed to
  use a linkpath whose parent directory doesn't exist (real ENOENT).
- Add mknod syscall support (AST + parser + codegen + coreasm macro):
  'Create a device node called "<path>" with type "c"|"b" major <n> minor <n>.'
  mode = S_IFCHR/S_IFBLK | 0666, dev = (major << 8) | minor
- Add tests: 087_mknod, 088_mknod_error

Full suite: 78/78 passing, no regressions.
